  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>420 Mules is a Maine medical cannabis delivery service operating in the Bar Harbor / Mount Desert Island region. Unlike the storefront dispensaries that dominate the rest of Maine's cannabis market, 420 Mules focuses on the medical delivery model — bringing registered patients their medicine rather than operating a walk-in retail location.</p>
    <p>This model is particularly well-suited to the Mount Desert Island region. Bar Harbor is small, the surrounding towns are sparsely populated, and Acadia National Park draws millions of summer visitors — but the registered medical patient base is dispersed across a wide geographic area. Medical delivery bridges that gap for patients who need regular access to their medicine without driving to a physical storefront.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>420 Mules serves the Mount Desert Island region and surrounding Hancock County. The primary service area includes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Bar Harbor</strong> (operator's home base)</li>
      <li><strong>Mount Desert Island</strong> — including Bar Harbor, Northeast Harbor, Southwest Harbor, Tremont</li>
      <li><strong>Trenton</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Ellsworth</strong> (mainland Hancock County)</li>
      <li><strong>Lamoine</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Sullivan</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Gouldsboro / Winter Harbor</strong></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Confirm the current service radius with the operator before placing an order. Maine's medical delivery rules require the patient to be a registered MMMP cardholder and the operator to hold appropriate caregiver or courier licensing.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to Order</h2>
    <p>420 Mules accepts orders through:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Official site:</strong> <a href="https://www.420mules.com/">420mules.com</a></li>
      <li><strong>Weedmaps listing:</strong> <a href="https://weedmaps.com/deliveries/420-mules">weedmaps.com/deliveries/420-mules</a></li>
      <li><strong>Direct contact:</strong> Phone available on the operator's site</li>
    </ul>
    <p>As a medical delivery service, 420 Mules requires the customer to be a registered Maine MMMP cardholder. Out-of-state medical patients from a reciprocity state should call ahead to confirm acceptance. The operator may also carry branded merchandise (shirts and sweatshirts) for sale on the website.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why a Delivery Model on Mount Desert Island</h2>
    <p>The Mount Desert Island region — home to Bar Harbor, Acadia National Park, and the surrounding coastal communities — has specific characteristics that favor the medical delivery model:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Geographic dispersion.</strong> Year-round population is small but spread across multiple towns and unorganized townships. A central storefront would be inconvenient for many patients.</li>
      <li><strong>Seasonal population swings.</strong> Summer tourism brings tens of thousands of visitors, but they are transient. The medical patient base is the year-round residents.</li>
      <li><strong>Limited retail cannabis zoning.</strong> Several Mount Desert Island towns have either opted out of cannabis retail or have restrictive local zoning that limits storefront dispensary operations.</li>
      <li><strong>Patient preference.</strong> For medical patients managing chronic conditions, home delivery reduces mobility barriers and provides predictable service.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Operators like 420 Mules are well-positioned to serve this market as Maine's medical cannabis program continues to grow.</p>
  </section>

